# PROJECT CHARTER: ENTERPRISE ERP CLOUD MODERNIZATION

> **Enterprise Practice:** Elsamag IT Solutions  
> **Lead Technical Consultant:** Samuel Chinwendu Agu  
> **Case Study Client:** Apex Global Distribution  
> **Project Title:** Enterprise ERP Migration Governance & Phase-Gate Control System  
> **Lifecycle Standard:** Hybrid Agile-Waterfall Phase-Gate Governance  
> **Document Identifier:** ART-01 | Project Charter v1.0  

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Business Case

### 1.1 Problem Statement
Apex Global Distribution’s core supply chain, warehouse management, and financial reporting workflows currently run on a 15-year-old on-premise ERP system. The legacy system exhibits high maintenance overhead, lack of real-time multi-region data visibility, performance degradation under peak load, and elevated security vulnerabilities.

### 1.2 Business Justification & ROI
Migrating to a modern cloud-native ERP platform will unify global operations, automate regulatory tax compliance, and reduce transactional latency. The projected return on investment (ROI) includes:
* **35% reduction** in infrastructure maintenance costs over 3 years.
* **40% acceleration** in end-to-end order processing and inventory reconciliation cycles.
* Real-time operational intelligence across all regional distribution nodes.

---

## 2. Project Objectives & Success Criteria (SMART)

| Objective Category | Specific Target Metric | Validation Method |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **System Availability** | Achieve 99.99% uptime for cloud ERP services post-cutover | Cloud monitoring telemetry |
| **Data Integrity** | Zero data loss during migration; reconciliation threshold $\ge 99.98\%$ | Automated ETL audit logs |
| **Schedule Adherence** | Complete cutover within the 24-week baseline window | Integrated Master Schedule (CPM) |
| **Budget Variance** | Total spend controlled within $\pm 1\%$ of authorized budget envelope | Earned Value Management (EVM) |
| **User Adoption** | 95% proficiency of supply chain and finance staff within 30 days of cutover | Training & assessment audits |

---

## 3. Project Scope Boundaries

### 3.1 In-Scope
* Migration of core business modules: General Ledger, Accounts Payable/Receivable, Inventory Management, Order Fulfillment, and Warehouse Management.
* Automated legacy ETL extraction, data transformation, cleansing, and multi-region staging.
* Integration with third-party logistics (3PL) carriers and regional tax engine APIs.
* User Acceptance Testing (UAT), security penetration testing, and role-based access control (RBAC) setup.
* Cutover execution, staff training curriculum, and post-go-live hypercare support.

### 3.2 Out-of-Scope
* Hardware upgrades for non-ERP related on-premise local workstations.
* Custom module development outside standard cloud ERP capabilities unless approved via formal CCB Tier 3 escalation.
* Historical transactional data archiving beyond the legally mandated 7-year retention window.

---

## 4. Milestone Schedule & Phase-Gate Governance

The program executes under a Hybrid Agile-Waterfall model featuring 4 mandatory Phase-Gates:

```text
[ Gate 1: Initiation ] ──► [ Gate 2: Planning ] ──► [ Gate 3: Execution ] ──► [ Gate 4: Closure ]
    Weeks 1 - 3                Weeks 4 - 8              Weeks 9 - 22              Weeks 23 - 24

Phase-Gate IDMilestone DeliverableExit Criteria
GATE-01: InitiationCharter Authorization & Scope Baseline100% Sponsor and Steering Committee sign-off
GATE-02: PlanningWBS, RACI & CCB Protocol BaselineBaselines locked; CCB voting quorum active
GATE-03: ExecutionSprint Iterations, Data Audit & UAT\ge 99.98\% data integrity; zero Tier 1 blockers
GATE-04: ClosureCutover, Runbook Handover & Post-MortemFormal acceptance sign-off; contracts closed
```

## 5. Governance Structure & Resource Allocation

### 5.1 Project Stakeholder & Authority Matrix

| Governance Role | Name / Title | Project Responsibilities |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Executive Sponsor** | VP of Operations, Apex Global | Ultimate budget authority, strategic escalation, and Gate 4 sign-off |
| **Lead Technical Consultant** | Samuel Chinwendu Agu, Elsamag | Governance oversight, CCB chair, schedule and architecture baseline management |
| **Enterprise Solution Architect** | Technical Lead | Cloud infrastructure design, API integration, and code quality audits |
| **Operations Process Owner** | Operations Lead | Business workflow validation, UAT coordination, and operational transition |
| **InfoSec & Compliance Officer** | Compliance Lead | Data protection, security audit compliance, and RBAC governance |

### 5.2 Budget & Funding Envelope
* **Authorized Program Budget:** $1,850,000 USD
* **Management & CCB Reserve:** $150,000 USD (controlled strictly via Change Control Board)
* **Funding Release Mechanism:** Milestone-gated disbursement upon successful passage of Gates 1, 2, and 3.

